  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given, current through the square loop is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/fd93c099-a7a1-4a47-82b0-d8529d10f77c-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 207px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></math></p><p>The given situation is shown in the figure. Magnetic field due to wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> at the centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> [Downward to the plane of square loop]</p><p>Since, magnetic field due to side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mi>A</mi></math> is same in magnitude and direction.</p><p>Hence, net magnetic field at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p>",
